      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like `download_mac_m1_toolchain.bzl` is using `xcode-select` to get the right directory here. Should this (here and below) be doing the same? Otherwise it may be possible for the headers and the tools to come from different places? More to the point, it looks like `download_mac_m1_toolchain.bzl` creates a symlink for to `usr`, should there just be a symlink for this based on `xcode-select` for `/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/Platforms/MacOSX.platform/Developer/SDKs/MacOSX.sdk` which would be the \"sdk symlink\"?\n\nI see that this is already the user\u0027s Xcode and not a hermetic one, but this should be set up so that it would \"just work\" if we switched to a hermetic one.",
      "revId": "b6e872974b82d7575887889994d2c67684b3e232",
